# Per-image build context for the agent PWA.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to `.dockerignore`,
# which is the only way one context can serve images that need different
# things. The root file excludes `apps/agent` and `apps/portal` so the API
# image does not carry two front-ends it never serves — correct for that
# image, and fatal for this one, whose entire source lives there. The build
# failed on `COPY apps/agent ./apps/agent` with "not found", because the
# context genuinely did not contain it.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backups
storage
docs
*.md
!README.md
apps/portal
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
